---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseHeader from '../../components/CaseHeader.astro';
import Turn from '../../components/Turn.astro';
import { project, views } from '@portfolio/content';
const p = project('hifi-player');
import { isPlaceholder } from '../../lib/placeholder';
const renders = ['hifi-rev1.png', 'hifi-rev2.png', 'hifi-rev3.png'].every((f) => !isPlaceholder(`assets/work/${f}`));
---
<Base
  title={views.caseTitle(p)}
  description={p.description}
  kind="work-case"
  depth={1}
  ground={p.ground}
>
<main id="main">

  <CaseHeader project={p}>

    <figure class="fig fig--bleed" id="fig-1">
      <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-1-cap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 130" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" overflow="visible" role="img" aria-labelledby="f1t">
          <title id="f1t">Audio path block diagram: a Bluetooth source and a microSD source, both under ESP32-S3R8 firmware, feed a MUX, which feeds an I2S DAC, which feeds the output.</title>
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/></marker>
          </defs>
          <!-- bracket over the two sources: y=22, x 0–140, 6px end ticks down -->
          <path class="crisp" d="M0 28 V22 H140 V28"/>
          <text x="0" y="14">ESP32-S3R8 firmware</text>
          <!-- boxes -->
          <rect class="crisp" x="0" y="32" width="140" height="36"/>
          <rect class="crisp" x="0" y="82" width="140" height="36"/>
          <rect class="crisp" x="240" y="57" width="90" height="36"/>
          <rect class="crisp" x="400" y="57" width="110" height="36"/>
          <rect class="crisp" x="580" y="57" width="70" height="36"/>
          <text class="t-ink" x="70" y="55" text-anchor="middle">Bluetooth</text>
          <text class="t-ink" x="70" y="105" text-anchor="middle">microSD</text>
          <text class="t-ink" x="285" y="80" text-anchor="middle">MUX</text>
          <text class="t-ink" x="455" y="80" text-anchor="middle">I2S DAC</text>
          <text class="t-ink" x="615" y="80" text-anchor="middle">out</text>
          <!-- sources converge on the MUX -->
          <line class="geo" x1="140" y1="50" x2="240" y2="75" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
          <line class="geo" x1="140" y1="100" x2="240" y2="75" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
          <!-- MUX → DAC → out -->
          <line class="crisp" x1="330" y1="75" x2="400" y2="75" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
          <line class="crisp" x1="510" y1="75" x2="580" y2="75" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="fig-1-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;1</span> — Audio path: Bluetooth or microSD, selected by a MUX, into an I2S DAC.</figcaption>
    </figure>

  </CaseHeader>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="prose-block col-full">

      <h2 class="col-head" id="brief">The brief</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">A battery-powered HiFi music player, started in May 2026 and designed end to end: schematic capture, a four-layer PCB layout, the power path, and firmware on an ESP32-S3R8.</p>
      <p class="col-prose">I wanted one project that went through every step of a real product board rather than a dev kit with wires: choosing the parts, drawing the schematic, laying out a 4-layer board with a proper power path for a battery, and then writing the firmware that makes it play music. A music player is a good vehicle for this; it is obvious when it does not work.</p>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="sources">Two sources, one DAC</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">Audio streams in from Bluetooth or from a microSD card. Either source is routed through a MUX into an I2S DAC (Fig.&nbsp;1). The ESP32-S3R8 handles both sources on the same chip.</p>
      <p class="col-prose">The board is four layers (Fig.&nbsp;2). The power path is designed for battery operation, so the whole thing was meant to leave the bench.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-2">
        <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-2-cap">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 800 200" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="img" aria-labelledby="f2t">
            <title id="f2t">Four-layer PCB stack-up in section: four copper layers L1 to L4 separated by three dielectric slabs, drawn at equal thickness because no thicknesses are stated.</title>
            <defs>
              <pattern id="hatch" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" width="7" height="7" patternTransform="rotate(45)"><line class="s-rule" x1="3.5" y1="0" x2="3.5" y2="7"/></pattern>
            </defs>
            <rect class="f-hatch" stroke="none" x="0" y="34" width="560" height="40"/>
            <rect class="f-hatch" stroke="none" x="0" y="78" width="560" height="40"/>
            <rect class="f-hatch" stroke="none" x="0" y="122" width="560" height="40"/>
            <rect class="f-cu crisp" x="0" y="30" width="560" height="4"/>
            <rect class="f-cu crisp" x="0" y="74" width="560" height="4"/>
            <rect class="f-cu crisp" x="0" y="118" width="560" height="4"/>
            <rect class="f-cu crisp" x="0" y="162" width="560" height="4"/>
            <text class="t-ink" x="576" y="37">L1</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="576" y="81">L2</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="576" y="125">L3</text>
            <text class="t-ink" x="576" y="169">L4</text>
            <text x="576" y="58">dielectric</text>
            <text x="576" y="102">dielectric</text>
            <text x="576" y="146">dielectric</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="fig-2-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;2</span> — Four-layer stack, schematic: layer assignment and thicknesses not shown.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="board">The board</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">This is the current layout as a 3D model, straight from the EasyEDA Pro export: <span class="nb">70.9 × 50.4 mm</span>, and <span class="nb">8.5 mm</span> deep with the parts on. It is the design file, not a photograph; nothing on it was ever assembled.</p>

      <figure class="fig fig--bleed board" id="fig-board" data-model="../assets/pcb/hifi-board.glb" data-label="The current HiFi player board as a 3D model. Drag, or use the arrow keys, to turn it.">
        <div class="board__stage">
          <img class="board__poster" src="../assets/pcb/hifi-board-cut.webp" width="1600" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The current HiFi player board rendered in 3D, seen from above at an angle: a blue board with the ESP32 and the other packages, four electrolytic capacitors in the middle, four buttons and the USB-C connector along the front edge, and a 7-pin header at the back.">
        </div>
        <p class="board__bar"><span class="board__status" id="board-status">still render · turning the model needs JavaScript and WebGL</span><button class="board__reset" type="button" hidden>reset view</button></p>
        <figcaption id="fig-3-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;3</span> — The current layout: the STEP export from EasyEDA Pro, converted to glTF with every component body kept. The model loads when the figure comes into view.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="revisions">Three revisions</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">The layout has been through three revisions{renders && ', and the renders (Figs. 4–6) show each one'}. Revision 1 is a small board with two buttons, a USB-C connector, a <span class="nb">3.5 mm</span> jack, a large rotary control and a 4-pin header.</p>

      {renders && (
      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-4">
        <img class="fig__img" src="../assets/work/hifi-rev1.png" width="766" height="559" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Rendered layout, revision 1: a small board with two buttons, a USB-C connector, a 3.5 mm jack, a large rotary control and a 4-pin header.">
        <figcaption id="fig-4-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;4</span> — Layout, revision 1 (render).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      )}

      <p class="col-prose">Revision 2 is a larger board that adds a Bluetooth module with its own crystal, four buttons, a microSD slot and the ESP32-S3R8 with its crystal.</p>

      {renders && (
      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-5">
        <img class="fig__img" src="../assets/work/hifi-rev2.png" width="939" height="699" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Rendered layout, revision 2: a larger board with a Bluetooth module and its crystal, four buttons, a microSD slot and the ESP32-S3R8 with its crystal.">
        <figcaption id="fig-5-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;5</span> — Layout, revision 2 (render).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      )}

      <p class="col-prose">Revision 3 has four mounting holes, with the module and the ESP32 on the left, the DAC section and the <span class="nb">3.5 mm</span> jack top right, two electrolytic capacitors and the power section in the middle, USB-C, microSD and a JST battery connector along the bottom edge, and a 7-pin screen header at the top.</p>

      {renders && (
      <figure class="fig fig--right" id="fig-6">
        <img class="fig__img" src="../assets/work/hifi-rev3.png" width="1415" height="989" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Rendered layout, revision 3: four mounting holes; the Bluetooth module and the ESP32 on the left, the DAC section and the 3.5 mm jack top right, two electrolytic capacitors and the power section in the middle, USB-C, microSD and a JST battery connector along the bottom edge, and a 7-pin screen header at the top.">
        <figcaption id="fig-6-cap"><span class="fig__no">Fig.&nbsp;6</span> — Layout, revision 3 (render).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      )}

      <aside class="pull">
        <p class="pull__kicker">constraint</p>
        <p>Four layers, a battery, and two audio sources sharing one DAC.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="col-head" id="not-done">Where it stopped</h2>
      <p class="col-prose">I stopped the project in October 2026 at the design stage, to put the time into a project I find more engaging. It stands as a design exercise without physical verification: the schematic and the layout are done, and nothing was assembled, powered or tested, so nothing on this page is a measured result.</p>
      <ul class="check col-prose">
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/><path d="M2 5 L4.5 7.5 L8 3"/></svg><span class="check__state">done</span>schematic capture</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/><path d="M2 5 L4.5 7.5 L8 3"/></svg><span class="check__state">done</span>4-layer PCB layout (three revisions)</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/></svg><span class="check__state">not built</span>power path bring-up</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/></svg><span class="check__state">not finished</span>ESP32-S3R8 firmware</li>
        <li><svg class="chk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect x=".5" y=".5" width="9" height="9"/></svg><span class="check__state">not built</span>board bring-up</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="col-prose">The layout exists in three revisions{renders && ' (Figs. 4–6)'}. No board was assembled or powered, so there are no photographs of a built board.</p>

    </div>

    <Turn slug={p.slug} />
  </section>

</main>
<script src="../../scripts/board.js"></script>
</Base>
